  "title": "A clearer front door for community projects",
  "summary": "January made Pollinations easier to explore while expanding text and image options and tightening the APIs behind them.\n\nThe rebuilt homepage made examples, integrations, and community work easier to find. The project directory gained categories, restored missing entries, and added a GitHub form for submitting apps.\n\nDeepSeek-V3, DeepSeek reasoning models, GPT-4o vision, Claude 3.5 Haiku, and Qwen Coder broadened the model choices. JSON mode, temperature forwarding, web-search defaults, and vision examples made those choices more usable.\n\nRequests began mapping to supported aspect ratios and defaulting to 1024×1024. Prompt handling was corrected to preserve Persian and other non-Latin text, while authorized requests gained a priority path around the regular queue.\n\nText and image request pacing, routing, and error handling were revised, with clearer JSON errors and more tests and instrumentation. Text feed events also stopped including requester IP addresses.",
